# Swan Compiler 2 — Target Backend
#
# Select and configure a backend from an explicit target triple and ABI.
# SVM remains target-independent until this boundary.
#
# Backend responsibilities:
# - Validate architecture, operating system, ABI, object format, and features.
# - Define target data layout, pointer width, alignment, and calling convention.
# - Lower generic SVM operations to target-supported machine operations.
# - Select instruction patterns and legalize unsupported operations.
# - Define register classes, constraints, and relocation models.
#
# Initial target families: x86_64, AArch64, ARMv7, RISC-V 64, WASM32, WASM64.
# A target is available only when its lowering and code emitter are implemented
# and tested. A recognized target name alone does not mean it is supported.
#
# Implementation status: contract; Compiler 1 backends are the behavioral
# reference and must be ported target by target.
